#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:2
#, no-wrap
msgid "git-daemon(1)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:5
#, no-wrap
msgid "NAME"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:7
msgid "git-daemon - A really simple server for Git repositories"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:9
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNOPSIS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:25
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"'git daemon' [--verbose] [--syslog] [--export-all]\n"
"\t     [--timeout=<n>] [--init-timeout=<n>] [--max-connections=<n>]\n"
"\t     [--strict-paths] [--base-path=<path>] [--base-path-relaxed]\n"
"\t     [--user-path | --user-path=<path>]\n"
"\t     [--interpolated-path=<pathtemplate>]\n"
"\t     [--reuseaddr] [--detach] [--pid-file=<file>]\n"
"\t     [--enable=<service>] [--disable=<service>]\n"
"\t     [--allow-override=<service>] [--forbid-override=<service>]\n"
"\t     [--access-hook=<path>] [--[no-]informative-errors]\n"
"\t     [--inetd |\n"
"\t      [--listen=<host-or-ipaddr>] [--port=<n>]\n"
"\t      [--user=<user> [--group=<group>]]]\n"
"\t     [--log-destination=(stderr|syslog|none)]\n"
"\t     [<directory>...]\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:27
#, no-wrap
msgid "DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:31
msgid ""
"A really simple TCP Git daemon that normally listens on port "
"\"DEFAULT_GIT_PORT\" aka 9418.  It waits for a connection asking for a "
"service, and will serve that service if it is enabled."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:37
msgid ""
"It verifies that the directory has the magic file \"git-daemon-export-ok\", "
"and it will refuse to export any Git directory that hasn't explicitly been "
"marked for export this way (unless the `--export-all` parameter is "
"specified). If you pass some directory paths as 'git daemon' arguments, the "
"offers are limited to repositories within those directories."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:41
msgid ""
"By default, only `upload-pack` service is enabled, which serves 'git "
"fetch-pack' and 'git ls-remote' clients, which are invoked from 'git fetch', "
"'git pull', and 'git clone'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:44
msgid ""
"This is ideally suited for read-only updates, i.e., pulling from Git "
"repositories."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:46
msgid "An `upload-archive` also exists to serve 'git archive'."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:48
#, no-wrap
msgid "OPTIONS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:54
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--strict-paths::`\n"
"\tMatch paths exactly (i.e. don't allow \"/foo/repo\" when the real path "
"is\n"
"\t\"/foo/repo.git\" or \"/foo/repo/.git\") and don't do user-relative "
"paths.\n"
"\t'git daemon' will refuse to start when this option is enabled and no\n"
"\tdirectory arguments are provided.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:61
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--base-path=<path>::`\n"
"\tRemap all the path requests as relative to the given path.\n"
"\tThis is sort of \"Git root\" - if you run 'git daemon' with\n"
"\t'--base-path=/srv/git' on example.com, then if you later try to pull\n"
"\t'git://example.com/hello.git', 'git daemon' will interpret the path\n"
"\tas `/srv/git/hello.git`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:67
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--base-path-relaxed::`\n"
"\tIf --base-path is enabled and repo lookup fails, with this option\n"
"\t'git daemon' will attempt to lookup without prefixing the base path.\n"
"\tThis is useful for switching to --base-path usage, while still\n"
"\tallowing the old paths.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:77
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--interpolated-path=<pathtemplate>::`\n"
"\tTo support virtual hosting, an interpolated path template can be\n"
"\tused to dynamically construct alternate paths.  The template\n"
"\tsupports %H for the target hostname as supplied by the client but\n"
"\tconverted to all lowercase, %CH for the canonical hostname,\n"
"\t%IP for the server's IP address, %P for the port number,\n"
"\tand %D for the absolute path of the named repository.\n"
"\tAfter interpolation, the path is validated against the directory\n"
"\tlist.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:82
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--export-all::`\n"
"\tAllow pulling from all directories that look like Git repositories\n"
"\t(have the 'objects' and 'refs' subdirectories), even if they\n"
"\tdo not have the 'git-daemon-export-ok' file.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:88
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--inetd::`\n"
"\tHave the server run as an inetd service. Implies --syslog (may be\n"
"\toverridden with `--log-destination=`).\n"
"\tIncompatible with --detach, --port, --listen, --user and --group\n"
"\toptions.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:96
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--listen=<host-or-ipaddr>::`\n"
"\tListen on a specific IP address or hostname.  IP addresses can\n"
"\tbe either an IPv4 address or an IPv6 address if supported.  If IPv6\n"
"\tis not supported, then --listen=<hostname> is also not supported and\n"
"\t--listen must be given an IPv4 address.\n"
"\tCan be given more than once.\n"
"\tIncompatible with `--inetd` option.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:99
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--port=<n>::`\n"
"\tListen on an alternative port.  Incompatible with `--inetd` option.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:104
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--init-timeout=<n>::`\n"
"\tTimeout (in seconds) between the moment the connection is established\n"
"\tand the client request is received (typically a rather low value, since\n"
"\tthat should be basically immediate).\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:109
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--timeout=<n>::`\n"
"\tTimeout (in seconds) for specific client sub-requests. This includes\n"
"\tthe time it takes for the server to process the sub-request and the\n"
"\ttime spent waiting for the next client's request.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:113
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--max-connections=<n>::`\n"
"\tMaximum number of concurrent clients, defaults to 32.  Set it to\n"
"\tzero for no limit.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:116
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--syslog::`\n"
"\tShort for `--log-destination=syslog`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:122
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--log-destination=<destination>::`\n"
"\tSend log messages to the specified destination.\n"
"\tNote that this option does not imply --verbose,\n"
"\tthus by default only error conditions will be logged.\n"
"\tThe <destination> must be one of:\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:124
#, no-wrap
msgid "stderr"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:129
msgid ""
"Write to standard error.  Note that if `--detach` is specified, the process "
"disconnects from the real standard error, making this destination "
"effectively equivalent to `none`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:129
#, no-wrap
msgid "syslog"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:131
msgid "Write to syslog, using the `git-daemon` identifier."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:131
#, no-wrap
msgid "none"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:133
msgid "Disable all logging."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:137
msgid ""
"The default destination is `syslog` if `--inetd` or `--detach` is specified, "
"otherwise `stderr`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:147
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--user-path::`\n"
"`--user-path=<path>::`\n"
"\tAllow {tilde}user notation to be used in requests.  When\n"
"\tspecified with no parameter, a request to\n"
"\tgit://host/{tilde}alice/foo is taken as a request to access\n"
"\t'foo' repository in the home directory of user `alice`.\n"
"\tIf `--user-path=<path>` is specified, the same request is\n"
"\ttaken as a request to access `<path>/foo` repository in\n"
"\tthe home directory of user `alice`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:150
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--verbose::`\n"
"\tLog details about the incoming connections and requested files.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:155
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--reuseaddr::`\n"
"\tUse SO_REUSEADDR when binding the listening socket.\n"
"\tThis allows the server to restart without waiting for\n"
"\told connections to time out.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:158
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--detach::`\n"
"\tDetach from the shell. Implies --syslog.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:162
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--pid-file=<file>::`\n"
"\tSave the process id in 'file'.  Ignored when the daemon\n"
"\tis run under `--inetd`.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:170
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--user=<user>::`\n"
"`--group=<group>::`\n"
"\tChange daemon's uid and gid before entering the service loop.\n"
"\tWhen only `--user` is given without `--group`, the\n"
"\tprimary group ID for the user is used.  The values of\n"
"\tthe option are given to `getpwnam(3)` and `getgrnam(3)`\n"
"\tand numeric IDs are not supported.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:174
msgid ""
"Giving these options is an error when used with `--inetd`; use the facility "
"of inet daemon to achieve the same before spawning 'git daemon' if needed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:181
msgid ""
"Like many programs that switch user id, the daemon does not reset "
"environment variables such as `$HOME` when it runs git programs, "
"e.g. `upload-pack` and `receive-pack`. When using this option, you may also "
"want to set and export `HOME` to point at the home directory of `<user>` "
"before starting the daemon, and make sure any Git configuration files in "
"that directory are readable by `<user>`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:189
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--enable=<service>::`\n"
"`--disable=<service>::`\n"
"\tEnable/disable the service site-wide per default.  Note\n"
"\tthat a service disabled site-wide can still be enabled\n"
"\tper repository if it is marked overridable and the\n"
"\trepository enables the service with a configuration\n"
"\titem.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:195
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--allow-override=<service>::`\n"
"`--forbid-override=<service>::`\n"
"\tAllow/forbid overriding the site-wide default with per\n"
"\trepository configuration.  By default, all the services\n"
"\tmay be overridden.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:204
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--[no-]informative-errors::`\n"
"\tWhen informative errors are turned on, git-daemon will report\n"
"\tmore verbose errors to the client, differentiating conditions\n"
"\tlike \"no such repository\" from \"repository not exported\". This\n"
"\tis more convenient for clients, but may leak information about\n"
"\tthe existence of unexported repositories.  When informative\n"
"\terrors are not enabled, all errors report \"access denied\" to the\n"
"\tclient. The default is --no-informative-errors.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:215
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"`--access-hook=<path>::`\n"
"\tEvery time a client connects, first run an external command\n"
"\tspecified by the <path> with service name (e.g. \"upload-pack\"),\n"
"\tpath to the repository, hostname (%H), canonical hostname\n"
"\t(%CH), IP address (%IP), and TCP port (%P) as its command-line\n"
"\targuments. The external command can decide to decline the\n"
"\tservice by exiting with a non-zero status (or to allow it by\n"
"\texiting with a zero status).  It can also look at the $REMOTE_ADDR\n"
"\tand `$REMOTE_PORT` environment variables to learn about the\n"
"\trequestor when making this decision.\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:219
msgid ""
"The external command can optionally write a single line to its standard "
"output to be sent to the requestor as an error message when it declines the "
"service."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:220
#, no-wrap
msgid "<directory>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:226
msgid ""
"The remaining arguments provide a list of directories. If any directories "
"are specified, then the `git-daemon` process will serve a requested "
"directory only if it is contained in one of these directories. If "
"`--strict-paths` is specified, then the requested directory must match one "
"of these directories exactly."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:228
#, no-wrap
msgid "SERVICES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:236
msgid ""
"These services can be globally enabled/disabled using the command-line "
"options of this command.  If finer-grained control is desired (e.g. to allow "
"'git archive' to be run against only in a few selected repositories the "
"daemon serves), the per-repository configuration file can be used to enable "
"or disable them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:237
#, no-wrap
msgid "upload-pack"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:242
msgid ""
"This serves 'git fetch-pack' and 'git ls-remote' clients.  It is enabled by "
"default, but a repository can disable it by setting `daemon.uploadpack` "
"configuration item to `false`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:243
#, no-wrap
msgid "upload-archive"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:247
msgid ""
"This serves 'git archive --remote'.  It is disabled by default, but a "
"repository can enable it by setting `daemon.uploadarch` configuration item "
"to `true`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:248
#, no-wrap
msgid "receive-pack"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:257
msgid ""
"This serves 'git send-pack' clients, allowing anonymous push.  It is "
"disabled by default, as there is _no_ authentication in the protocol (in "
"other words, anybody can push anything into the repository, including "
"removal of refs).  This is solely meant for a closed LAN setting where "
"everybody is friendly.  This service can be enabled by setting "
"`daemon.receivepack` configuration item to `true`."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:259
#, no-wrap
msgid "EXAMPLES"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:260
#, no-wrap
msgid "We assume the following in /etc/services"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:265
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$ grep 9418 /etc/services\n"
"git\t\t9418/tcp\t\t# Git Version Control System\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:267
#, no-wrap
msgid "'git daemon' as inetd server"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:271
msgid ""
"To set up 'git daemon' as an inetd service that handles any repository "
"within `/pub/foo` or `/pub/bar`, place an entry like the following into "
"`/etc/inetd` all on one line:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:276
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\tgit stream tcp nowait nobody  /usr/bin/git\n"
"\t\tgit daemon --inetd --verbose --export-all\n"
"\t\t/pub/foo /pub/bar\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:279
#, no-wrap
msgid "'git daemon' as inetd server for virtual hosts"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:284
msgid ""
"To set up 'git daemon' as an inetd service that handles repositories for "
"different virtual hosts, `www.example.com` and `www.example.org`, place an "
"entry like the following into `/etc/inetd` all on one line:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:292
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\tgit stream tcp nowait nobody /usr/bin/git\n"
"\t\tgit daemon --inetd --verbose --export-all\n"
"\t\t--interpolated-path=/pub/%H%D\n"
"\t\t/pub/www.example.org/software\n"
"\t\t/pub/www.example.com/software\n"
"\t\t/software\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:300
msgid ""
"In this example, the root-level directory `/pub` will contain a subdirectory "
"for each virtual host name supported.  Further, both hosts advertise "
"repositories simply as `git://www.example.com/software/repo.git`.  For "
"pre-1.4.0 clients, a symlink from `/software` into the appropriate default "
"repository could be made as well."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:302
#, no-wrap
msgid "'git daemon' as regular daemon for virtual hosts"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:306
msgid ""
"To set up 'git daemon' as a regular, non-inetd service that handles "
"repositories for multiple virtual hosts based on their IP addresses, start "
"the daemon like this:"
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:312
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\tgit daemon --verbose --export-all\n"
"\t\t--interpolated-path=/pub/%IP/%D\n"
"\t\t/pub/192.168.1.200/software\n"
"\t\t/pub/10.10.220.23/software\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:318
msgid ""
"In this example, the root-level directory `/pub` will contain a subdirectory "
"for each virtual host IP address supported.  Repositories can still be "
"accessed by hostname though, assuming they correspond to these IP addresses."
msgstr ""

#. type: Labeled list
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:319
#, no-wrap
msgid "selectively enable/disable services per repository"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:324
msgid ""
"To enable 'git archive --remote' and disable 'git fetch' against a "
"repository, have the following in the configuration file in the repository "
"(that is the file 'config' next to `HEAD`, 'refs' and 'objects')."
msgstr ""

#. type: delimited block -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:329
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\t[daemon]\n"
"\t\tuploadpack = false\n"
"\t\tuploadarch = true\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:333
#, no-wrap
msgid "ENVIRONMENT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:338
msgid ""
"'git daemon' will set REMOTE_ADDR to the IP address of the client that "
"connected to it, if the IP address is available. REMOTE_ADDR will be "
"available in the environment of hooks called when services are performed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title -
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:340
#, no-wrap
msgid "GIT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/git-daemon.txt:341
msgid "Part of the linkgit:git[1] suite"
msgstr ""
